{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/copy_shared_7.march","start_line":14,"start_col":22,"end_line":14,"end_col":24,"message":"`List.map` builds a new copy instead of reusing `xs` in place, because `xs` is used again afterwards.\nA function can update a value in place only when it holds the only reference to it; make this call the last use of `xs` and `List.map` reuses its memory instead of allocating.","code":"copy_shared","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/copy_shared_7.march","start_line":15,"start_col":24,"end_line":15,"end_col":26,"message":"`xs` is used again here, so it is still shared when `List.map` runs"}],"notes":[],"category":"COPY"}
